WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.776
Hannah: Uncertain commits need lookup by idempotency key.

2
00:00:04.776 --> 00:00:08.568
Anika: We've matched all acknowledged requests to orders.

3
00:00:08.568 --> 00:00:11.927
Lukas: What about writes without a client acknowledgment?

4
00:00:11.927 --> 00:00:16.919
Raj: Some committed before disconnect. That's expected, right?

5
00:00:16.919 --> 00:00:22.007
Hannah: Yes. A timeout doesn't mean transaction failure.

6
00:00:22.007 --> 00:00:26.039
Priya: Let me play that back. Look up first.

7
00:00:26.039 --> 00:00:30.359
Raj: The last committed position supports acknowledged-write coverage.

8
00:00:30.359 --> 00:00:33.670
Lukas: But don't rule that out for unacknowledged gaps.

9
00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:37.582
Anika: Just to recap, retries can catch up safely.

10
00:00:37.582 --> 00:00:43.390
Priya: With deduplication, yes. Perhaps manual review for exceptions.

